{"name":"Rocket Science","hex":"#ff3311","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rocket science","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The science or study of rockets and their design.","Anything overly complex, detailed, or confusing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocket_science"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocket Science Games","blocks":[{"text":"Rocket Science Games was a video game developer and publisher that created games for consoles and personal computers from 1993 to 1997. The company released Loadstar: The Legend of Tully Bodine, Cadillacs and Dinosaurs: The Second Cataclysm,\nWing Nuts: Battle in the Sky, Rocket Jockey, and Obsidian. The Space Bar was the final game developed by Rocket Science. After the company folded, it was published by SegaSoft. Six additional games were never completed."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/49/Rocket_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Science_Games","wikidata":"Q7355138"},{"title":"Rocket Science (film production company)","blocks":[{"text":"Rocket Science is an independent film production, financing and sales company based in the United Kingdom."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Science_(film_production_company)","wikidata":"Q137258601"},{"title":"Rocket Science (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rocket Science is a 2007 American comedy-drama film written and directed by Jeffrey Blitz, and starring Reece Thompson, Anna Kendrick, Nicholas D'Agosto, Vincent Piazza, and Aaron Yoo. It tells the story of Hal Hefner, a fifteen-year-old stutterer who decides to join his school's debate team when he develops a crush on its star member, and addresses the themes of coming of age, sexuality, and finding one's voice."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Rocket-science.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Science_(film)","wikidata":"Q821753"},{"title":"Rocket","blocks":[{"text":"A rocket is an elongated flying vehicle that uses a rocket engine to accelerate without using any surrounding air. A rocket engine produces thrust by reaction to exhaust expelled at high speed. Unlike jet engines, rockets are fuelled entirely by propellant which they carry, without the need for oxygen from air; consequently a rocket can fly in the vacuum of space, and indeed rocket engines operate more efficiently outside the atmosphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg/330px-Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket","wikidata":"Q41291"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/AnnaKendrick09TIFF.jpg/500px-AnnaKendrick09TIFF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/AnnaKendrick09TIFF.jpg/500px-AnnaKendrick09TIFF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anna Kendrick learned debate strategies and studied with a college debate coach to prepare for the role","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnnaKendrick09TIFF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Jeffrey_Blitz.jpg/500px-Jeffrey_Blitz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Jeffrey_Blitz.jpg/500px-Jeffrey_Blitz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jeffrey Blitz drew from many of his own experiences as a stutterer when writing the script.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJeffrey_Blitz.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Rocket_Science_still.jpg/330px-Rocket_Science_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Rocket_Science_still.jpg/330px-Rocket_Science_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A drab color palette was used to give the film a deadpan undertone.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARocket_Science_still.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg/330px-Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg/330px-Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rocket arrows depicted in the Huolongjing: \"fire arrow\", \"dragon-shaped arrow frame\", and a \"complete fire arrow\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rocket_warfare.jpg/500px-Rocket_warfare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rocket_warfare.jpg/500px-Rocket_warfare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mysorean rockets and rocket artillery used to defeat an East India Company battalion during the Battle of Guntur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARocket_warfare.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg/250px-William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut